# Native semantic weights: foundation and controls

The native Need frontier instantiates the free resumption handler and its
finite-arity operation theory. Coefficient erasure recovers ordinary execution;
ordered factor ledgers preserve sharing; declared readouts obey the common
scope-descent boundary. Exact rational complex coefficients use Mathlib's
quadratic algebra, with cancellation and future-interference controls.

Native event receipts and the existing operational Cost schedules use the same
indexed valuation interface. Captured local-cell views reuse finite revision
dependencies; quoted-work folds reuse certified catalogue accessibility and an
independent dependency-derivation judgment.

Finite-worker costs retain both worker placement and sequential phase
boundaries, including nested child spans and several children on one worker.
Containing receipt scopes deduplicate live destinations, and successful finite
identity reservations preserve each ledger's freshness frontier. Ordinary
parameter frames share one release law for arbitrary finite argument lists.
The interleaved reservation protocol retains each invocation's expected value
and finished result through retries. Successful comparisons derive freshness;
scoped delivery retains only successful identities in issuance order. Spurious
failure proves neither exhaustion nor eventual service. Atomic source and
physical ledger publication retain separate correspondence obligations.
Observed sequential ledgers retain numerical counters independently of their
chronology. Identity or storage refusal makes history permanently incomplete,
while cumulative work, per-kind counters and sequential span keep charging.
The complete-history readout justifies reconstruction only on complete
receipts; the common fibre obstruction rules it out for incomplete receipts.
Numerical inspection also exposes the retained prefix and incompleteness flag.
It returns the preceding observation and then charges its own read; repeated
inspection and failed retention keep that distinction. A complete resulting
history agrees with the independently specified unbounded read operation.
Child imports use the same ledger: complete children replay their exact events,
while incomplete children contribute their independent numerical counters.
Mixed imports preserve the retained prefix after the first refusal. The common
worker-phase schedule supplies span without reconstructing it from work or
from an incomplete event history. Equal-valued child states remain separate
physical imports; admitting each owner once is a distinct runtime obligation.
The admitted C counter route implements the independent work coordinate, with
the enclosing append, storage and identity services still requiring refinement.
The native counter helper is admitted from complete C source by
the shared reader and proved against independent natural-number saturation.
Its scalar, sequential memory profile is separate from whole-ledger and
concurrent worker refinement.

The actual receipt wrapper is admitted with its declared services. Under a
state-preserving inactive query it returns zero, restores the complete caller
state and never invokes observed accounting. Runtime overhead and the service
implementations retain separate obligations.

Copied residual storage uses the common injective address and payload
relocation. Complete paths and aliases are preserved and reflected, and
cursor publication retains duplicate answer occurrences while counting their
shared graph once. Cancellation commutes with relocation; copying work is
separate from the retained-byte account.

Prepared operations reuse the private-write batch kernel and original
stateful controller. Physical completion can precede parent selection without
changing the ordered prefix or complete residual. The native instance checks
executable paths within the original program and initial-machine scope;
strict invalidation retains the snapshot and prepared operation. Speculative
expenditure and C service refinement remain separate obligations.
Bounded checkpoints also retain the whole remaining preparation/publication
continuation and cumulative parent-tick count. Refusal leaves that checkpoint
intact; split execution equals combined execution, with the native full
snapshot determined by accepted parent ticks. Finishing preparation alone
does not certify search exhaustion.

Pending coefficients use the actual native score computation and retain its
completed choice world when the body resumes. Unannotated contributions take
the direct path with no additional grading step. Declared coefficient admission
uses that same continuation and filters before the body executes. At every
finite budget its complete occurrence list is a sublist of attachment-only
execution, preserving the surviving coefficients, order and open worlds.
Admission is enabled only at completed authored coefficients; arbitrary
predicates retain exact unannotated same-budget execution, including those
that reject the administrative unit coefficient.
Boolean OR/AND controls distinguish false rejection, true admission and an
uninterpreted score; nonzero numerical admission preserves shared lazy choices
and duplicate physical answers. Unfinished scores remain open. Nested
coefficient continuations also retain annotations on arguments forced while a
grade runs. They restore the exact parent instruction with the child's world
and work. Identity controls distinguish this from ordinary unweighted scoring:
two binding-local grades of seven contribute forty-nine, including when the
outer grade forces the inner argument. The richer stack keeps the original
same-budget unannotated execution. Settled and nested adapters share one free
finite-arity operation construction and its independently executed weighted
linear reading; scalar linearity remains restricted to commutative scalars.
The instruction meter accounts for the body, active grade and retained
parents. Actual instruction counts cannot decrease and remain bounded by
the quantum allowance; returning a child transfers its account once.
The list of owned frame counts determines this readout, while the retained
body alone does not: equal bodies at two real cuts have different totals.
This Need-instruction profile is separate from runtime event costs and
cost-observation expense.
The resource guard's complete
C invocation implements the common collective demand inequality and releases
its parameter cells without altering caller state.

The common resource search rediscovers candidates in each descendant world.
Complete catalogues justify terminal publication; bounded execution retains
the full frontier. Its MeTTa-calculus instance executes actual guarded
transactions, including directives created by earlier continuations. Ordered
firing histories and their commuting trace classes remain different views.

This entry point covers those mathematical interfaces. The C coefficient
frames, selector loop, reflected ledger and concurrent workers retain their
separate source-correspondence obligations.
